---
layout: page
title: Key Locations
---

<!-- Index of all location pages. Pages register themselves by carrying a
     location_type (geographic | symbolic) in their front matter. -->

<p>
  Every week's overview lists the key locations for that week's readings. The
  pages gathered here go deeper: what each place was in the first century, what
  happened there, and a photograph of the site as it looks today. Locations that
  are not places on a map -- visions, heavenly settings, figures of speech --
  are illustrated with historic artwork instead, always labeled as an artist's
  interpretation.
</p>

<%
  locs = site.collections.pages.resources
             .select { |r| r.data.location_type }
             .sort_by { |r| r.data.title.to_s }
  geographic = locs.select { |r| r.data.location_type == "geographic" }
  symbolic   = locs.select { |r| r.data.location_type == "symbolic" }
%>

<h2>Places</h2>
<ul class="location-index">
  <% geographic.each do |loc| %>
    <li>
      <a href="<%= relative_url loc.relative_url %>"><strong><%= loc.data.title %></strong></a>
      <% if loc.data.blurb %><span class="location-index-blurb"><%= loc.data.blurb %></span><% end %>
    </li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<% unless symbolic.empty? %>
<h2>Beyond the Map</h2>
<ul class="location-index">
  <% symbolic.each do |loc| %>
    <li>
      <a href="<%= relative_url loc.relative_url %>"><strong><%= loc.data.title %></strong></a>
      <% if loc.data.blurb %><span class="location-index-blurb"><%= loc.data.blurb %></span><% end %>
    </li>
  <% end %>
</ul>
<% end %>
